@format 1
@id queue.claim-work
@title Claim queued work
@area Queue
@entry input
@summary Select the next eligible pending item, move it to running state, and establish ownership and lease data.
@flow TB
@allow-cycle true
@related processing.run-job
@tag queue
@tag claim
@tag lease

@alias schedule = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSchedule
@alias store = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LScheduleStore

[input] Worker requests work <input>
- Request the next item for a runner identity @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
> order

[order] Order candidates <process>
- Read all scheduled work records @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
- Order high-priority work first and then by creation time @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
> candidate

[candidate] Check next candidate <decision>
- Apply the cohort gate to the candidate batch @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
? "Candidate cohort is eligible" > move
? "Candidate cohort is held" > candidate [loop]
? "No candidates remain" > none

[move] Acquire running-file claim <decision>
- Move the record from scheduled to running storage @ store.LScheduleMove(...)
? "Move succeeds" > own
? "Another process wins or move fails" > candidate [loop]

[own] Establish ownership <storage>
- Set running state, process identity, runner identity, lease time, phase, and attempt count @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
- Save the owned record in running storage @ store.LScheduleRecordSave(...)
- Register the live running item and record the claim @ schedule.LScheduleClaim(...)
> claimed

[claimed] Work claimed <output>
= The caller receives one running work item after its file move. If ownership metadata cannot be saved, the claim remains runnable but may be reclaimed after lease expiry.

[none] No claim <output>
= The caller receives no work item.
